# Content diversity (no archive sequels)

Each new article is a **new topic**, not a relative of an existing post.

## Orchestrator / claim
- `scripts/claim-next-topics.mjs` must claim unused named candidates (novel themes first).
- Never mint `{theme}-update-*`, `{theme}-concentration-*`, `{theme}-geography-*`, or `{theme}-cycle*` sequels of a theme that already has posts.
- Do not instruct workers to write a companion, vintage delta, or "same question, new quarter" cut.

## Worker / subagents
- The assigned brief is the whole idea. Do not survey `src/data/posts.ts` `content:` fields for inspiration.
- When registering the new post, copy **object keys only** from one existing entry; write original prose and a new visualization.
- If you spawn subagents, give them only this brief + source URLs. Do **not** paste existing article bodies, sibling slugs, or "look at how we did the last concentration post".
- Forbidden framing: "Our theme already maps", "companion to", "vintage slope versus last print", "the July research put…".
- Internal links: 0 or 1. Zero is better than a sequel chain.
- Do not clone another post's dashboard layout (KPI row + one bar chart).

## Why
The conveyor previously filled idle slots with update/concentration/geography variants of the same ~20 themes. That made the archive a hall of mirrors. New work must look like a different magazine issue, not the same chart with a new date.
